From f298637c81ad6be4c018742d8bd89f5d6ad884e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:16:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): draw the simulated tool as the revolved outline
 the collision laws judge

The tool at the playhead is now one revolved body built from the two
reads the fixture laws make: the judged tool record for the cutter and
shank, and the band stack (`tool_body::stack`) above it - the holder
cylinder, an imported body's revolved envelope (#368) or a drawn
holder's bands (#93). Before, a tool with a body drew the body's own
facets, which no law reads.

The mesh is cached for the one tool at the playhead, keyed by its
outline, and dropped when the tool, its operation or the transport is
gone. A degenerate or misfitting tool draws nothing and is logged by
name. Display only: no verdict and no posted output changes.

Part 2 of #743 (STEP body to an editable DXF half-profile) is not in
this commit.

Refs #743

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
